RESULT
------
3 ERROR(S):
  E1. Round-start anchor contradiction on 31 rounds (R2-R32): the construction notes say 'work the first dc or BO into the SAME stitch as the join', but the round text says 'in next st', which starts one stitch past the join.
  E2. Simulated consequence: the 12 increase/bobble columns rotate by 120.8 degrees from R1 to R32 - the 'snowflake' spirals instead of radiating. Stitch counts stay correct, so a count-only checker cannot see this.
  E3. stated yarn 700-1200 g is far above the simulated requirement (standard 217-260 g, large 398-478 g). A maker would buy roughly 2-3x too much yarn.

3 WARNING(S):
  W1. claimed hole 1.5-2.0 in does not contain the simulated relaxed value 1.25 in (R1's 12 dc gather the ch 20 ring from 15.8 cm down to 10.0 cm)
  W2. R32: simulated finished diameter 42-45 in is not covered by the printed 38.0-43.0 in
  W3. gauge is measured on a 'flat swatch' but quoted in 'rounds'; say 'rows'

1 NOTE(S):
  N1. R14 (a size stopping point) is a bobble round, so a few edge bobbles fall inside the border's 'skip 2'. Cosmetic only; an extra plain round before the border avoids it and keeps the 12N/2N maths.

FAIL - correct the errors above before publishing.

